.TH MD_DELETE 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_delete \- destroy a decoder and release its storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

void md_delete(morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Destroy a decoder and release its storage.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Handle to destroy. NULL is accepted and has no effect.
.SH RETURN VALUE
This function returns no value.
.SH REMARKS
Stops and joins all workers before releasing owned buffers and the FFT plan.
The handle and any borrowed
character views are invalid after return. This does not flush pending
decoding: call md_flush() and consume final snapshots before deletion if final
output is required. Deleting the same non-NULL handle twice is invalid.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Exclude all concurrent use of this handle. Serialize destruction with every
FFTW planner and plan-destruction operation in the application.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_new (3),
.BR md_new_iq (3),
.BR md_flush (3)
